.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-harvest-id 1  "id " 
.SH NAME
git\-harvest\-id \- Register and maintain the CHANGELOG\*(Aqs contributor registry
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-harvest id\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-changelog\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register and maintain the CHANGELOG\*(Aqs contributor registry.
.PP
Wraps four registry operations — `inherit`, `register`, `update` and `merge` — used to keep the registry accurate as people join, change their Git identity, or need two recorded identities folded into one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-changelog\fR \fI<CHANGELOG>\fR [default: CHANGELOG.ron]
The CHANGELOG whose contributor registry is edited
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
git\-harvest\-id\-inherit(1)
Register the identity from the local Git configuration
.TP
git\-harvest\-id\-register(1)
Register a contributor under a chosen alias
.TP
git\-harvest\-id\-update(1)
Change a registered contributor\*(Aqs names, e\-mails or URLs
.TP
git\-harvest\-id\-merge(1)
Fold several registered contributors into one
